secureshellgo (1.2.0~noble5) noble; urgency=medium

  * Revert `dart pub get --enforce-lockfile --offline` back to
    `flutter pub get --offline`. The dart CLI doesn't set up
    FLUTTER_ROOT the way the flutter wrapper does, so `dart pub get`
    can't resolve `flutter_test` (which comes from `sdk: flutter`,
    not pub.dev) — ~noble4 failed with "the Flutter SDK is not
    available." The extended strip that covers both .pub-cache and
    .flutter/packages already stops the workspace expansion that
    broke ~noble3; the enforce-lockfile flag was over-engineering.

