secureshellgo (1.2.0~noble4) noble; urgency=medium

  * Extend the `resolution: workspace` strip to include the vendored
    Flutter SDK's own package pubspecs (flutter_test, flutter_
    localizations, integration_test). The ~noble3 build got past the
    `dart pub get --enforce-lockfile --offline` step but then failed
    inside `flutter build linux --release --no-pub` with the same
    socket error — the workspace declaration in flutter_test's
    pubspec.yaml (which our app depends on as a dev dep) pulled its
    dev_dependencies (`test`, `test_core`) into the resolution.

 -- Dhiva Labs <dhivakar1010@gmail.com>  Thu, 30 Jul 2026 19:40:00 +0530

secureshellgo (1.2.0~noble3) noble; urgency=medium

  * Fix offline pub resolution failing on Launchpad ("Got socket error
    trying to find package test at https://pub.dev." under --offline).
    Three defensive fixes because the root cause is Launchpad-specific
    and would not reproduce locally:
    - Touch pubspec.lock before pub get: dpkg-source preserves mtimes,
      so a version bump can leave pubspec.yaml newer than pubspec.lock
      and trigger pub's "lockfile stale" re-resolution.
    - Strip `resolution: workspace` from every pubspec in the vendored
      pub cache: ten transitive deps (test_api, meta, ffi, win32...)
      declare it, which pulls each package's dev_dependencies (`test`,
      `test_core`) as if they were monorepo members.
    - Use `dart pub get --enforce-lockfile --offline` instead of
      `flutter pub get --offline`: --enforce-lockfile forbids any
      resolution that would change the lockfile, which forbids any
      network fallback even under workspace expansion. Only exposed
      through the dart CLI.

 -- Dhiva Labs <dhivakar1010@gmail.com>  Thu, 30 Jul 2026 13:30:00 +0530

secureshellgo (1.2.0~noble2) noble; urgency=medium

  * Vendor the Flutter SDK and pub cache under packaging/vendor/ so the
    build no longer needs outbound network access — the previous
    ~noble1 upload failed on Launchpad because debian/rules tried to
    curl the Flutter SDK from storage.googleapis.com, which the build
    farm blocks.
  * Drop curl, unzip and ca-certificates from Build-Depends; nothing in
    the build reaches the network any more.

